{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city","id":662429,"title":"The City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-12T17:30:04-07:00","id":662429,"title":"The City","content":"So, a while (several years come to think of it) I started this grandiose project ... it has been a weird trip trying to write it, but fun none the less. Over the last few months the writing bug has hit and i have been slowly editing, re-writing and finishing sections off, especially those that dealt with the strange new stuff I was adapting and bringing in. Some you will remember me talking in the corner about this project, long conversations with the clock and the designs on the wall, which of course has all helped write it. It is not done by far but it is actually proceeding well for a change. I have a couple of the chapters finished, and even pdf-ed to look all nice and glam. I am going to google doc the lot of it for people to see and comment on. Go nuts.. blow me out of the water or give me suggestions, hints, rule breaks etc. I will post as I update sections and so those who are interested can see and who knows even use some of it.<br /> <br /> I am going to start with Chapter Three which is now pretty much done and looking all nice and glitzy. Over the coming week I will add links to the other chapters as well as the maps of the city for people to see what I am slowly driving myself insane writing ... :P<br /> <br /> <br /> Ignore the link below .. use the big listing further down the page ... i just can`t figure out how to remove the link completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":722,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","user":"Walksforever","date":". 08-17-2017, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T17:33:35-07:00","id":662453,"title":"","content":"one of those links will likely not work right .. sigh ... need coffee","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T17:38:42-07:00","id":662460,"title":"","content":"The first one works right. You can edit the post so you don't have to make new ones. This looks really cool, nice job with the formatting. I haven't done more than skim so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T20:22:50-07:00","id":662606,"title":"","content":"So anything marked done is pretty much, well, done. Not saying refinement and touch isn't needed, and suggestions and such are extremely welcome. Anything noting WIP no longer has a link, unless it has a bevy of content that is in a sorta readable state. In some cases all I have is a page of point form notes and ideas. If someone wants to see that, let me know and I will post it to be seen. I will be relinking PDFs over the next couple of days.<br /> <br /> Timeline -- WIP\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VKvvyenuBfSPpJmDQPB43LTpWFIg3Gr_/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Prologue</a>-- Done\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1r309a_D1ugR4K81UbwMtuBW8Vkf7lb0s/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Introduction </a>-- Done<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BOf9bXkPoq5YCwYIuIUvASQ-K7PQx1cF/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter One: Geography</a> -- Almost done, some areas still need fleshing out<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TCbesNBlrGdI-2tMZk8aZGxNtsPuvqi0/edit?usp=share_link&amp;ouid=109446409111211068316&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Two: History</a> -- Almost done, needs some expanding on certain periods though, so expect it be updated<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16V1QjQAwXRITC12ZjcfN-rfCg28OZiSt/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Three: Deadly Seas</a> -- Done<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1t91ABRXA6Mi94v3EeBuq9vdz4cEZERoF/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Four: Whispers in the Dark</a> -- 80%<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RvWy63kXX6Dv4cJNsCwGq542QoqhdT4Q/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Five: Small Town Blues</a> -- 90%<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17-c8OGTSQNTozy1U5MI6eOT6SYJXw7P_/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Six: Moonlit Streets</a> -- 90%<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d22ymHZBo27AZC7uY9KChTfUdeRdnYRh/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Seven: A Scream from the Depths</a> -- 90%<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uyIkG-BVraCjxwzoufUrAe_QYNppSRLL/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Eight: The Never Ending Show</a> -- WIP<br /> Chapter Nine: Nature Trail to Hell -- WIP<br /> Chapter Ten: Red Legacy -- WIP<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NAoOuxHWr_VuI-LjyChp1iy5HrSaN1Cl/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Eleven: Eternal Nights</a> -- Done<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rSVZiyR2I4l_cFIjwYLpB5SBw26wNn5N/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter Twelve: Kindred of the City</a> -- Done<br /> Chapter Thirteen: Savage Moon -- WIP<br /> Chapter Fourteen: Forsaken of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Fifteen: Mind over Matter -- WIP<br /> Chapter Sixteen: Awakened of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Seventeen: The Forever Path -- WIP<br /> Chapter Eighteen: Created of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Nineteen: Lost and Found -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty: Lost of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-One: Light in the Dark -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-Two: The City\u2019s Vigil -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-Three: Chthonian Dreams -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-Four: Geist of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-Five: Sands of Time -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-Six: The Arisen of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-Seven: Cogs in the Machine -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-Eight: Unchained of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Twenty-Nine: Waking Nightmares -- WIP<br /> Chapter Thirty \u2013 Begotten of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Thirty-One: Fearful Symmetry -- WIP<br /> Chapter Thiry-Two: Remade of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Thirty-Three: Hell on Earth -- 80%<br /> --- Map of the wasteland reflection of the City<br /> Chapter Thirty-Four: Taken of the City -- 70%<br /> Chapter Thirty-Five: Islands in the Sky -- WIP<br /> Chapter Thirty-Six: Exiles of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Thirty-Seven: Concrete Jungle -- WIP<br /> Chapter Thirty-Eight: Primals of the City -- 70% done<br /> Chapter Thirty-Nine: Silent Death -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty: Inquisitors of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty-One: Children of the Gods -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty-Two: Scions of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty-Three: Tarnished Gold -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty-Four: Exalted of the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty-Five: To Be Inspired -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty-Six: The Continuum in the City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty-Seven: The Shadow City -- WIP<br /> Chapter Forty-Eight: Shadows of Shadows -- WIP<br /> End Word<br /> Appendix 1: Social Charts<br /> Appendix 2: Maps of the City<br /> City Districts<br /> Index of the map<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-W9i6abvJZx20U__9tXnRcM5Vfg5R-Q4/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">FEAR Corporation</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/152-yUh4AMNxljwoiwHAhsXA3HoolPhR-/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Project NOVA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Y8ghB0B0Idf_FNAG7VVSa34xd3NRt_Z/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Rival Corporations</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uia_ALEH49xK9fANbuH-G8eqh7fC1KCr/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\">Foundation for Law and Home Security</a><br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":722,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","user":"Walksforever","date":". 03-21-2023, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:27:12-07:00","id":663156,"title":"","content":"Ok .. there it is at the moment .. as I update and write I will and remove. All comments, ideas, flames, suggestions, OMGs, WTFs and such are appreciated. If I can keep my brain going my plan is to have alot of it done by Xmas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:20:56-07:00","id":667450,"title":"","content":"For the Exiles, you appear to be drawing inspiration from <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b> and heavily modifying it to reflect a more religious interpretation. If I got that right, I would recommend looking at <b>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</b> as well: I'm pretty sure that one of Dark Ages developers indicated that <b>Inquisitor</b> was intended to be that line's counterpart to <b>Reckoning</b>. In particular, I'd note that <b>Inquisitor</b> used Conviction in a role not unlike a \u201cpower stat\u201d and used \u201cPiety\u201d in a role akin to a \u201cmorality stat\u201d. They were definitely different things, with too much Conviction and not enough Piety resulting in a state of Callousness. <br /> <br /> Consider making the Exile's Power Stat be Conviction while leaving his Morality Substitute as Communion, and have a similar dynamic between the two as exists between Conviction and Piety in <b>Inquisitor</b>. Faith as a fuel stat still makes sense, though it would be derived from Conviction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:53:31-07:00","id":667608,"title":"","content":"The weird thing was I was trying to figure out a way to do the Exiles when someone on the forums suggested using the old HtR stuff .. so I did .. but yeah heavily modifying to a degree. I will go pull the DA stuff and take a look as well. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T20:05:23-07:00","id":671626,"title":"","content":"Been working slowly on updates here and there ... will endeavor to update the google docs Sunday. Had a thought about the Exiles ... perhaps the reason the Seraphim take the Grigori is not only to watch but also to defend against the \u201couter gods\u201d in a war to stop them from invading. Grigori are also tasked with seeking out the cults of these old gods and destroying them to limit the faith that pours up and into their aether to sustain them in their dark places. When exiled the Exiles fight to return to assist or to return to take over and run the war properly, but many fall to the outer gods, becoming minions of their strange cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T08:59:30-07:00","id":680062,"title":"","content":"Going over the newer GMC rules in detail ... did the facepalm as i realized i'd not updated to them .. sigh ... lol .. the project that never ends!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T09:41:10-07:00","id":680084,"title":"","content":"Found something that could help with your brainstorming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UbuNd0A030k\" data-code=\"UbuNd0A030k\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UbuNd0A030k/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T08:28:38-08:00","id":765572,"title":"","content":"Cool vid. I am hoping to update stuff this weekend.. sorry about the delays .. work has been less than stellar to me and has my brain in a bad place ... that and Fallout4 and Legacy of the Void came out ... :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T10:11:55-08:00","id":765631,"title":"","content":"No worries; take your time man. Enjoy yourself with the new releases and see what inspiration they may or may not bring for when you're back on track, until then there is no rush so don't stress yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T17:27:38-08:00","id":771924,"title":"","content":"OK so... I a having a wee bit of hard time doing the Forsaken part atm. I want the beginning to read like stories and songs that might told by the Uratha. Not sure I am quite hitting it. <br /> <br /> This what I have so far ... <br /> <br /> <i> Let me tell you a story of the world and how it was sundered.</i> Once, long ago, everything was one, and the spirit and the flesh walked together, watched over by Father Wolf. Pangea. It was our Eden. Then there came the fall, when our ancestors saw Father Wolf falter and so they took it upon themselves to save the world by replacing him, and upon slaying him did they realize that they had done more harm than good, forever destroying our paradise.<br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> <i>This is a tale of how the world was in the lands that were.</i> Once the land was fresh, covered in the might of the wild and open to skies from which the stars looked down upon us. All was in order, with life moving as it should. The people had recovered from the sundering and now lived with those of their kin and their kins\u2019 kin. We were rare in those days in this land of the past, born to the blessed of Luna and raised by kin in the ways of the tribe. We hunted the lands for fresh kill, sharing with the people and kin. We sang songs about the fire, danced under the moonlight and sought to honor our ancestors and forget the deeds of the first born which sundered all.<br /> We discovered other shifters in our travels across the lands, like us, few and far between, and we also discovered the Hosts as we wandered. Rage and jealously led to many battles between the people and the other shifters and hosts. Our numbers were depleted even more when we encountered our brothers the Pure. Territories we drawn, tribes formalized and lines drawn. We strove to hold onto what little we had left and rebuild the people.<br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> The Forsaken are a curious breed, wolfen shapeshifters, half in the spirit world, half out. They have existed for untold thousands of years, indeed if some were to be believed since the dawn of creation, once the guardians of the borders between worlds; they were cast down for killing their sire. As least that is what they believe.<br /> The Forsaken inhabited the area where the city is for hundreds, perhaps thousands, of years before the founding of the city. They lived off the land, paying homage to the spirits of the wild as they did so, making sure to appease the good spirits who brought them bountiful harvests and game. The songs tell how the Uratha that lived within them were viewed as gifts from the spirits, their children given to the tribes through mortal man to be raised to help understand man, so that when they died and joined the spirits they would better understand man and his ways. Native American legends and stories of shapechangers exist throughout their songs and stories of the past. In many cases these are based on interactions with either Forsaken or other shapechangers.<br /> <br /> <i> We sing tonight about a time of darkness.</i><br /> In nights past<br /> Dark brothers walked<br /> Shadows behind them<br /> Blood in their eyes<br /> <br /> Manitou of death claimed the children<br /> Manitou of shadow chilled the souls of the elderly<br /> Manitou of disease and pestilence walked among us<br /> Kin grew sick and many became duguthim<br /> The lucky died<br /> <br /> The people rose<br /> Walking under the stars<br /> Their howls echoing the forests<br /> Shattering the Manitou and dark brothers wills<br /> Claw and fang torn into corrupted flesh and souls<br /> <br /> The new dawn shone<br /> Light warming cold souls<br /> Sending the dark brothers back to the shadows<br /> A time of healing again began<br /> <br /> Early in the history of Uratha in the area they ran afoul of a pack of <i>Azah Gadar</i>, the Bale Hounds, who came to make war upon the peaceful people of the area. They unleashed horrors on the tribes and corrupted many, sowing the seeds of possession by dark and powerful manitou. These Bale Hounds were defeated by the sacrifice of many, the foul horrors forced back into the spirit realms and the Uratha set to guard them. The lore of the local Uratha tells how a mighty forest grew up around the place of passage, full of mighty trees and imbued with a strange supernatural life of its own, utterly wild and untamable. The songs and tales tell of many years of peace, with Uratha and man living happily, the land providing them with plentiful harvests and long summers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Let me tell you of a time when winter did not want to leave.</i> The people and their kin had enjoyed many seasons of bountiful harvests and game. They had grown, spreading out across the land with many small villages that traded with each other. Life was good and peaceful. The first signs of the coming cold were the lessening of the harvests. Crops didn\u2019t grow enough due the shortened seasons but luckily most villages had surplus and so they shared and didn\u2019t think much about it. Game became scarce next, with the lack of fresh growth in the grasses and trees, the deer and other plant eaters grew thin and sparse. The predators followed suit, in some cases destroying entire herds to sustain themselves to the determent of the people and their kin.<br /> Then came the cold and snows and ice that seemed to never leave. Many moved southwards to escape the frigid onslaught while others stayed, determined to survive the cold winters. Among the people a young Uratha came forward have claimed to have been given a vision of the sun being trapped by a vast shadow like thing that sapped and ate its light and strength. At first the youth was scoffed at, but when two others stepped forwards saying they too had seen the vision, it was taken as a sign that the spirit of the sun was under attack and that the three would be the ones to free it. The youths purged and readied themselves through rituals and rites for their journey, gathering powerful medicines and fetishes to carry with them. <br /> They entered the Shadow and began their journey, walking deep into the places that were but whispers in the tales of old. Many challenges came before the youths as they travelled, from having to play word games with powerful nature spirits, to bargaining with ice spirits to see which side they might be melting on, which would reveal from where the sun\u2019s rays came, to finally hiding from the spirit of something that took the form of Father Wolf, calling itself the Winter Wolf, the Harbinger of Fimbulwinter and the first of the three messengers of the End Times. The tales of these trials are for another night as they teach other lessons.<br /> Finally the youths reached the shadowed realm of the sun itself, where the vast shadow was slowly encircling the spirit in its folds. Coated in frost with ice hanging from their fur, the youths engaged the shadow with gifts of light while using gifts of fire and heat on the fading sun. The sun, sensing the aid, sparked one final time and its power combined with the youth\u2019s energy re-ignites it and the sun flared to life in all its glory, banishing the shadow to the depths of the Shadow.<br /> The youths returned to their tribes as the snows melted and the ice receded, the plants springing to life again.<br /> This story is true.<br /> <br /> The time of cold occurred deep into the past of the world, with many occultists and researchers noting it might coincide with the last mini ice age. The whole spirit quest to free the sun is something many tales exist of, with variations on what trials the youths had to overcome to get to the sun spirit, but the one which is always the same is that of the Harbinger of Fimbulwinter appearing, something that many deem to be a foreshadowing of times to come. Modern Uratha doubt that the spirit quest occurred, citing it as pure fantasy, but the older members, especially those of Native American descent, all say it did happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T18:26:43-08:00","id":771960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the spirit of something that took the form of Father Wolf, calling itself the Winter Wolf, the Harbinger of Fimbulwinter and the first of the three messengers of the End Times.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Storm Lords are not pleased by this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T07:46:27-08:00","id":772299,"title":"","content":"hmmmm ... going back over my lore.. missing something ... need to read more of the intro &quot;this story is true&quot; stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T12:01:04-08:00","id":774177,"title":"","content":"Hey, just wanted to give words of encouragement to this project. This is a great project and you're doing fantastic work, I'm using parts of this for my own city in Hunter.<br /> <br /> Can I request what part to see next, please? The biggest part I'm using is the Geography so the New City part would be really appreciated, I've been running mostly sessions in the slums so far. How's it going with the New City content?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4662-xanbai","name":"Xanbai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:27:37-08:00","id":774531,"title":"","content":"hmmm .. mostly its just &quot;jotted notes&quot; so to speak but i will upload some updates and see what i can post for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T17:09:54-08:00","id":776892,"title":"","content":"Ok. I just updated the City Timeline, Chapters 1, 2, 11, 12, 13 and 14, as well as the Intro section. Its all still a WIP atm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T18:08:04-08:00","id":776910,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;Lone&quot; Wolf as a replacement name/something to build a concept over in place of Winter Wolf in case you haven't already? The idea being that werewolves as well as the Firstborn and their Spirit packs all form in groups for their hunts and are always surrounded by others, especially social connections and prey.<br /> <br /> Lone Wolf would be a solitary godmonster representing an antithesis to this dynamic. Representing not just being alone in the sense you are separated from others you care about, but you are isolated from ...everything, perhaps not on a physical level, but spiritually primarily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T18:51:05-08:00","id":776931,"title":"","content":"I have to give you kudos on the Exiles (Grigori) splat in there, it's buried gold, and very interesting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T08:01:16-08:00","id":777150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city?p=776910#post776910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about &quot;Lone&quot; Wolf as a replacement name/something to build a concept over in place of Winter Wolf in case you haven't already? The idea being that werewolves as well as the Firstborn and their Spirit packs all form in groups for their hunts and are always surrounded by others, especially social connections and prey.<br /> <br /> Lone Wolf would be a solitary godmonster representing an antithesis to this dynamic. Representing not just being alone in the sense you are separated from others you care about, but you are isolated from ...everything, perhaps not on a physical level, but spiritually primarily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm ... an interesting idea. I will toss it on the idea pile with the others I have for that chapter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city?p=776931#post776931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to give you kudos on the Exiles (Grigori) splat in there, it's buried gold, and very interesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Can't claim all the credit. For one, its a re-hash of the Hunter the Reckoning stuff, for another the idea came from another member of the forums who suggested to try it as the basis for the Exiles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T10:53:40-08:00","id":777821,"title":"","content":"going to post up links to as much of the other WIP stuff i have as well .. that way you can see where i am going with some of it ... of course some of it will likely change and is merely place holders for ideas and such i had when writing. Its like a big puzzle and I am trying to fit it all together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T12:56:12-08:00","id":777870,"title":"","content":"Hey, this is great! I spend most of my idle daydreaming thinking about doing something like this, so you actually doing it is a big inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:52:00-08:00","id":779036,"title":"","content":"OK .. mass update. I have updated almost every file with new stuff. It is all WIP. Some of it (like the Arisen and Beasts) is bare as bones ... the Demon section too. I've not got to them heavily yet. Other stuff is near pdf creation so they look like a couple of the pdf docs in here. All comments welcome. Let me know where it doesn't make sense, or i've forgotten a rule or made a mistake with the lore or mechanics... juggling all these pieces sometimes gets kinda mucky in the brain. <br /> <br /> Enjoy and please let me know what you think<br /> <br /> I hope to keep the updates more frequent ... though the Fallout 4 monster keeps tackling me ... speaking of which .. its breathing over my shoulder now ... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:46:03-08:00","id":779193,"title":"","content":"Great progress! I'm currently transferring quite a bit of this into my own world especially the Never Ending Show part. My city is a casino city so it's a good fit. Keep up the good work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4662-xanbai","name":"Xanbai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:42:07-08:00","id":779841,"title":"","content":"Anything in particular about it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T09:33:47-08:00","id":779881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city?p=779841#post779841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything in particular about it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the casinos for one, I can take your three straight out of the box and place them on the board. My notes actually had a couple of Seer pylons so we're in sync with that. Was wondering how to include changelings as in my current history they've been all but wiped out. but you've answered that for me. Excellent idea with the God Machine, what I've done is folded Portsmith into the city itself and linked the slot machine infrastructure to the clock tower infrastructure in your timeline. Sadly I can't put the casinos on the river as by the time I realised putting two sides of the city on separate sides of the river (the Thames) was a good idea the game had already launched.<br /> <br /> Interesting choice with the Sin-Eater Krewes, no less than five in one area. I'm trying to fit that into the current game but that means I'll have to invent 20-25 NPCs if I use all five krewes.<br /> <br /> <br /> While I'm here I'll tell you my current supernatural composition in this area: Seers under the guise of finance and Russian gangsters, vampires, Ashwood Abbey variant, the Arisen meret from Mummy Ready Made Characters and Knights of Saint George. A demon lord is making waves in the area as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4662-xanbai","name":"Xanbai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T10:48:55-08:00","id":779942,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> Oh.. for those that haven't seen them, I've added links to the FEAR CORP stuff in the big doc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T08:59:22-08:00","id":788139,"title":"","content":"Bit of a slow down atm .. work and the xmas season. I am happy to see Onyx continuing with the Wo... I mean Chronicles of Darkness. I am going to have to modify my stuff now lol .. more updating lol, sigh, tis the season. I hope to have some updates in before next week for you all. It will likely be just little things, updates to the 4 new types of supernaturals, the outer realms they are part of and those borderlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T13:53:25-08:00","id":789910,"title":"","content":"I just posted the possible finished Introduction chapter, which formating, pics and such. Let me know what you think. <br /> <br /> Check it on the main post or the link here <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bzp045TvTWAibWtNbFVMdkF3bTA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bzp045TvTWAibWtNbFVMdkF3bTA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bzp045TvTWAibWtNbFVMdkF3bTA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bzp045TvTWAibWtNbFVMdkF3bTA/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T19:54:17-08:00","id":790058,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Of Supernal Realms, Hedges and my Cosmology of the World of Darkness&quot; section on the third page appears to be cut off mid-sentence, before the next section (&quot;How to use this fan supplement&quot;) starts. I initially assumed it was misplaced during formatting, though a second reading has convinced me that the &quot;How to use this fan supplement&quot; is an insert. This would be clearer if the 'How to' text box had visible borders.<br /> <br /> Will now check page 4+, please keep up the good work. Very appreciative.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: A few minor grammer errors, (missing full stops and the like); but came across something more significant. Just got to the Education section of the Departments/ Dept. Heads section. It is not a complete sentence. Housing may only have one line but at least it makes sense. the description for education is just a list of the types of schools one might expect - not even stating that they can be found in the City. It is not even a complete list; neither primary or high schools are listed (let alone that weird jr. High that apparently exists).<br /> <br /> While the following places of note is nice and certainly more useful, I wish the generic section was more like the one for Health &amp; Emergency Medical Services or at least Housing...<br /> <br /> Also (FU) is meant to be (EU) yes? Harrison College doesn't have a second rivalry with an undetailed school; or is Edward University shortened to FU for some reason? If so, can the reason be detailed somewhere (another chapter is fine, just kind of useful).<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Werewolf section this time; Focus instead of Locus, I assume this is a 'local' preference. Maybe mention that sometimes the other name gets used somewhere (either in the Hisil/spirit/shadow chapter or one of the werewolf ones would be fine).<br /> <br /> Also the Shadow section has a typo I think should be cleaned up before it's done. For simplicity, I'll just bold the typo in this quote.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter0b - Introduction, The City Project</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For more information on <b>Oddities</b> in the City, see Chapter 40: The Shadow City.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 12-21-2015, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T21:55:11-08:00","id":790090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city?p=790058#post790058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Of Supernal Realms, Hedges and my Cosmology of the World of Darkness&quot; section on the third page appears to be cut off mid-sentence, before the next section (&quot;How to use this fan supplement&quot;) starts. I initially assumed it was misplaced during formatting, though a second reading has convinced me that the &quot;How to use this fan supplement&quot; is an insert. This would be clearer if the 'How to' text box had visible borders.<br /> <br /> Will now check page 4+, please keep up the good work. Very appreciative.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: A few minor grammer errors, (missing full stops and the like); but came across something more significant. Just got to the Education section of the Departments/ Dept. Heads section. It is not a complete sentence. Housing may only have one line but at least it makes sense. the description for education is just a list of the types of schools one might expect - not even stating that they can be found in the City. It is not even a complete list; neither primary or high schools are listed (let alone that weird jr. High that apparently exists).<br /> <br /> While the following places of note is nice and certainly more useful, I wish the generic section was more like the one for Health &amp; Emergency Medical Services or at least Housing...<br /> <br /> Also (FU) is meant to be (EU) yes? Harrison College doesn't have a second rivalry with an undetailed school; or is Edward University shortened to FU for some reason? If so, can the reason be detailed somewhere (another chapter is fine, just kind of useful).<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Werewolf section this time; Focus instead of Locus, I assume this is a 'local' preference. Maybe mention that sometimes the other name gets used somewhere (either in the Hisil/spirit/shadow chapter or one of the werewolf ones would be fine).<br /> <br /> Also the Shadow section has a typo I think should be cleaned up before it's done. For simplicity, I'll just bold the typo in this quote.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks for the heads up on the mistakes ..I shall correct those right now and re-pdf it. Most of them are just me being stupid and not catching them in an edit as well as forgetting proper terms for stuff. Sigh. Brain full of the new Star Wards movie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The FU was because originally it was going to be Franklin University ... then I had a mental picture of the school jacket with FU on it ... and thought nahhhhhh. lol<br /> <br /> Let me know about anything else please and thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":722,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","user":"Walksforever","date":". 12-21-2015, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T22:24:51-08:00","id":790102,"title":"","content":"Is okay. Everyone has tired brain fails. Will do second run through later - have holiday stuff to do","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T22:56:56-08:00","id":790699,"title":"","content":"Updated the PDFs for the Prologue and Intro. The Geography and History sections will take a bit to do atm. Going to go over Chapter 3 and re-do the PDF. Hope to have the PDFs for Chapters 4 and 5 by xmas for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":722,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","user":"Walksforever","date":". 12-22-2015, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T22:20:31-08:00","id":792568,"title":"","content":"Updated the Prologue, Intro and Chapter 3 to be more inline with the new Chronicles of Darkness. Also added Chapter 4 pdf..... Merry Xmas everyone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T10:33:21-08:00","id":801490,"title":"","content":"I've added in the pdf near final version of Chapter Five. Took a break over the holidays. Hop to be back on track with Chapter 6 this week. Happy new year everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T21:54:20-08:00","id":817396,"title":"","content":"Writers block ... sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T14:06:07-08:00","id":834031,"title":"","content":"So trying to break through the writers block .. been wacking away at the Cemetery... i have some prelim stuff i did.. two Mage legacies and an Arisen cult and they are very rough .. any thoughts?<br /> <br /> <b>Mages \u2013 The Awakened</b><br /> Awakened have often remarked that the quiet nighttime of the Graveyard is perhaps one of the nicer things of the entire place. With connections to the Underworld to be had, and wealth of knowledge to be found in the tombs, the Awakened tend to see the Cemetery as one giant archaeological dig. The Awakened soul is immune to the effects of the Cemetery.<br /> Those of the Moros path have an affinity to this place and are more likely to be found here exploring than any other of the paths. A few Apostates have learned that the Cemetery is a good hiding spot, using a local graveyard\u2019s Death Gate as a way to hide from both Pentacles and Seers. Members of the Stone Scribes legacy have been spotted in the Cemetery from time to time as well, digging through the ruins, tombs and mausoleums, searching for artifacts to study. Two legacies have also been found to have had their origins here, the Death\u2019s Eyes and the Stygian Knives, a left handed legacy of soul stealers.<br /> <br /> <b>Death\u2019s Eyes</b><br /> <br /> <i>The dead leave many stories untold and so we search for them, to record them, pass them on, learn from them and grow from their knowledge and teachings.</i><br /> <br /> This legacy is based out in the Cemetery, seeing it as the perfect place to learn the state of death. Many of the legacy are looking into the secrets that were left by the Reapers and the Inquisitors, hunting for answers about what happened to the Outer Realm and border march that connects it to the Fallen World. They hunt for their answers with the dead interred within the border march and the spirits that still exist here.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Dead Heads<br /> <b>Orders:</b> The Mysterium<br /> <b>Appearance: </b> Those of this legacy tend to be rather pale, having spent a lot of time in the Outer Realm of Stygia. Most members are obsessively clean, though they tend to have a slight aroma of fresh earth about them.<br /> <b>Background:</b> For those Moros mages who find the lure of death overwhelming, some decide that to best experience death, the outer realm of Stygia is perhaps a good place to study. This realm is in what many of the Moros path described as permanent state of death, stuck in that moment before going onwards to whatever exists beyond death. For those that decided to push their understanding, the Death\u2019s Eyes legacy is a home for them to learn in.<br /> <b>Organization:</b> Moros of this legacy tend to working solitary environments, tucked away in their studies in small havens either deep within the outer realm of Stygia or in small easily missed homes in the Fallen World. The typical Stygian haven is a usually a Bolthole that has been secured, warded and properly shored up with defenses. Most of these locations are full of stacks of paper and artifacts gleaned and excavated from the ruins around them, as well as possibly small rooms dedicated to dissection and proper examination of the flora and fauna of the outer realm. Members of this Legacy are not unsocial, and many of them maintain personal contact with other members of the legacy as well as other Awakened and sleepers on a regular basis. Those rare Death\u2019s Eyes that loose themselves to the outer realm stop being members of this legacy and become something different, something of the left-handed legacy known as the Stygian Knives (see later).<br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Thanking the spirits of the dead, leaving tokens of respect on graves.<br /> <b>Concepts: </b>Spiritualist, mortician, seeker of truth<br /> <b>History</b><br /> This legacy and its dark twin brother have their origins deep in the past and indeed, many are not quite sure when they first were created. Some obscure texts have references to the legacy during the time of the old kingdom in Egypt, while others are noted from even earlier in the history of man, with death cults among the Awakened who had travelled to the outer realm of Stygia.<br /> Over the centuries the legacy took form as a way for Awakened to study death, but it wasn\u2019t till the destruction of the border march and vanishing of the servants of the enigmatic Reapers that the legacy started to actually find itself. The strange death like state of the outer realm let the legacy push itself, creating its final attainments, but sadly it also saw the birth of its left-handed twin, the Stygian Knives.<br /> In the modern nights those of this legacy are often sought out for their knowledge of death in all its forms, seen as keepers of esoteric knowledge.<br /> <b>Society and Culture:</b> For the Awakened of this legacy death is nothing new, indeed it is something to be studied, respected, embraced and researched. Many of the members of the legacy are physicians of some type, using their medical knowledge as a way to enhance their skills and talents. Death Eye\u2019s keep in contact in the Fallen World though all modern means from emails and chat groups to cell phones. Groups meet with other members of the legacy as well as other Moros path Awakened whenever they feel the need. The legacy is not seen as harmful and while albeit sometime they are viewed as bit weird, most Awakened have no issues with those of this legacy.<br /> <b>Induction:</b> Joining into this legacy is actually rather an easy task for any of the Moros path. The simple desire to learn more about death will often lead the perspective student to seek out a member of the legacy who is usually fairly happy to teach others about their way.<br /> <br /> <b>Magics</b><br /> Tomb Gate (Space 3)<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (target number = current gauntlet rating)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Transitory (1 turn)<br /> <b>Aspect: </b>Vulgar<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Mysterium Rote:</b> Dimension Door<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b><br /> The mage learns how to create a portal from the Fallen World into one of the outer realm borderlands, in this case the Cemetery. Variations of this magic can create quick short lived portals into any of the borderlands, though for the Moros who walk the path of the Death\u2019s Eyes, it is Tomb Gate they learn so that they can enter the Cemetery. Of note is the variations of this spell the allow Awakened access to the other borderlands. This spell only accesses the Cemetery.<br /> <br /> <b>1st:</b> Walking the Paths<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Death 1<br /> In order to find out information, secrets, stories, indeed anything, the mage must know where to look and where to dig in the vast border land that is the Cemetery. This attainment links the mage with the realm allowing him to slowly gain insight into where to go and look. <br /> This attainment allows for the mage to focus and meditate on what he is searching for. As he sits, letting his mind commune with the border march, he slowly gains an understanding as to where to look for this information. Initially it is merely a glimmering of the location, something that allows them to make the journey there and know when they are within the area. As they progress with their attainments this location information becomes more accurate.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Fate 1<br /> Those mages with Fate can use it help pinpoint the exact spot the information is contained at once they have gotten the general location from the initial mediation. This cuts the time to locate the item at its physical location in half.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd:</b> Hearing the Whispers<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Death 1<br /> The dead are not truly dead, they say, merely in a transitional state, readying themselves before the spirit moves onwards to the next incarnation or to heaven or hell, or whatever maybe. The dead talk. They whisper endlessly to themselves and the other dead. They argue, talk, sing, scream, cry and even create, depending on their state of mind, so to speak. The mage at this point in his attainments is able to tune into the cacophony of whispers, hearing them everywhere around him. By concentrating he can try to localize down to a single whisper. Once done, the mage listens for stories, secrets, information and other tidbits. With practice the mage is able to trace the whispers from conversation to conversation, listening to entire debates that happen among the dead of the Cemetery and Stygia. <br /> <br /> <b>3rd:</b> Dead Speak<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Death 5<br /> This attainment actually allows the mage to bring forth the dead, enjoying into conversations with them in order to ask questions directly. The mage must have information on the dead person he is trying to contact, including the location of their grave or tomb in the Cemetery or Stygia. Each dead person is different and they range from the calm and rational to the psychotically insane.<br /> It should be noted that the dead of the Cemetery and Stygia can be somewhat difficult to deal with, and have been known to rise from their graves to deal with upstart living things that disturb their sleep. <br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Spirit 5<br /> Those with both Arcana are actually able to bring the dead of the Cemetery to life to aid them in a pinch. With a roll of Presence + Persuasion + Spirit against the local dead\u2019s Resistance, the dead will rise and aid the mage as needed for a scene.<br /> <br /> <b>The Stygian Knives (Left Handed Legacy)</b><br /> <br /> <i>We alone know who has been given the divine gift. We alone know who has to be brought home. We alone here the call and we alone will answer it with the souls of the gifted.</i><br /> <br /> Among the Legacy known as the Death\u2019s Eyes are a few who answer a different call, becoming Stygian Knives. These strange awakened believe that they are serving a divine power, killing those that need to be killed and bringing their souls back to the Cemetery so they can be released into the border march to be sent to Stygia.<br /> The Stygian Knives operate quietly, inducting members from only the Moros path who answer the call the Death\u2019s Eyes legacy, which makes them doubly rare. The Knives use ritual blades forged of a material known as soulsteel (said to be made from their own souls), to kill their targets and trap their souls to be release later. With each soul successfully brought to Stygia the Knives add a ritual scar to their body marking their path on their so call divine way.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Soul Stealers<br /> <b>Orders:</b> The Mysterium and the Guardians of the Veil<br /> <b>Appearance: </b> Like the legacy that they spawned from, the Stygian Knives are generally pale skinned from the time they spend in Stygia. Most member have ritual scars across their arms, chest, back and legs as well.<br /> <b>Background:</b> For every ten members of the Death Eye\u2019s legacy, one might turn to the left-handed legacy known as The Stygian Knives. These confused awakened see that it\u2019s there duty to bring death to those that deserve it and need it, then bring their souls to Stygia where they belong.<br /> <b>Organization:</b> The Stygian Knives operate as a loose cult, with members freely joining with other member when needed for missions and information sharing, as well as for rituals such as the induction of new members and the release of those souls brought to Stygia.<br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Returning souls to Stygia, marking new scars<br /> <b>Concepts: </b>Spiritualist, ritual murderer, cultist<br /> <b>History</b><br /> This left-handed legacy came into being shortly after the destruction of the Cemetery and the vanishing of the Reaper\u2019s servants. For some reason some of the Death\u2019s Eye\u2019s newer members wandered off, vanishing into the Cemetery. No one is quite sure what it is that causes this to happen, though a couple of the Stygian Knives have been noted as saying they were answering the call.<br /> In the modern nights the Stygian Knives are a rare left-handed legacy, but are considered extremely dangerous.<br /> <b>Society and Culture:</b> The Knives have a cult like society, following strange rituals for finding their targets as well as when a target\u2019s soul has been released. Ritual scarring is a common method for this legacy to show progress in their learning of attainments, given by other members of their legacy in small, almost casual meetings where they gather and tell stories.<br /> A first scar is given when the Knife is inducted, the second when he forges his blade, after that scars are given when souls are released, or great acts are done, and of course when they attend the death of a fellow Knife. The scars are made by other Knives as stories are told and are intricate and details, no two being the same. It is said that if one could possible decipher the scars it would tell the story of the Knife\u2019s life and death.<br /> Knives spend their time between hunts, operating very much like those of the Death\u2019s Eyes legacy, researching the dead, sifting through the ruins for artifacts and knowledge and other such tasks. Of course much of this is for them to find the name of their next target. These targets could be anyone, from sleepers to other Awakened to any number of other supernaturals, as long as there is a \u201csoul\u201d to be taken.<br /> Once a target is found, the Knives hunt their target down and the chosen Knife kills the target with his blade, trapping the soul in it. There could be one target, or many, and usually it is not uncommon to have a number of Knives equal to the target plus two on a hunt, though solitary hunts are done. The Knives return to the Cemetery and travel to the edge of the border march and Stygia. Here the gathered Knives place the blades which hold souls in to a small fire then recount the deed by which they took the souls. As each does this they will the blade to release the soul, which slowly rises then moves off towards Stygia. No one is sure what happens to the souls when they reach Stygia.<br /> <b>Induction:</b> No one is sure what calls one to the Stygian Knives. Those rare members who have been captured speak of a call, not really a voice or song, just a call that they follow till they meet more Stygian Knives, usually at a small gathering. Here the prospective Knife is inducted into the legacy and given his first ritual scar, after which he will either witness a soul being sent onwards, the crafting of a soulsteel knife or the choosing of a target. It is just as likely he will merely sit around a fire and trade stories of life and death with those around him. Regardless, after the meeting the new Knife goes off with one of the older Knives to learn his new craft. <br /> Two weeks after the first meeting the new Knife will go through the process of having his own soulsteel knife forged. This rite, while simply done, is quite distinctive and dramatic, especially to the Knife upon which it is done. All Knives go through this process. Over the course of a night of storytelling of the kills made by the other Knives the gather Awakened slowly draw forth a piece of the soul of the initiate Knife. This piece of their soul is melded into a piece of ore dug from the land in the Cemetery, then forged into a blade through the use of magicks by the initiate and the gathered Knives. The Knife will then carry this blade with them till their death.<br /> <br /> <b>Magics</b><br /> Tomb Gate (Space 3)<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (target number = current gauntlet rating)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Transitory (1 turn)<br /> <b>Aspect: </b>Vulgar<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Mysterium Rote:</b> Dimension Door<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b><br /> The mage learns how to create a portal from the Fallen World into one of the outer realm borderlands, in this case the Cemetery. Variations of this magic can create quick short lived portals into any of the borderlands, though for the Moros who walk the path of the Death\u2019s Eyes, it is Tomb Gate they learn so that they can enter the Cemetery. Of note is the variations of this spell the allow Awakened access to the other borderlands. This spell only accesses the Cemetery.<br /> <br /> <b>1st:</b> Freeing the Soul<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 3, Death 3<br /> This attainment allows the Knife to trap the departing soul of the target they have killed in their soulsteel blade. This is similar to the Sever the Sleeping Soul spell, but where that one takes the soul from a living target, this one is only usable on the dying, and only on the chosen target. No mana is spent and a Presence + Intimidation + Death roll is required versus the dying person\u2019s Resolve. There is no benefit from the trapped soul, it is merely trapped in the blade till released. Mortal souls are easy to take, but supernatural souls are more difficult and generally most will not be able to be trapped unless the wielder has reached the third attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd:</b> Bonds of the Legacy<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Spirit 4<br /> The mage is able to harness the energy of those fellow knives around him, gaining strength and power. Each Knife who is present in the hunt can add a bonus to all their combat and perception rolls, as well as casting rolls equal to the number of hunting party divided by 2, rounded down, to a max of 5. This bonus will also apply to Paradox rolls.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum: </b>Death 4<br /> If the mage is also has Death 4 he can drain the essence and power of his fellow hunt members to gain even more power, using their life to fuel himself in his effort to kill the target and save the soul. This act is usually an agreed on thing, as the hunt members freely give their lives to the primary to help him. For each hunt member that links themselves to the primary like this, the primary ignores wounds and wound penalties, as well as tilts and conditions, as they are instead transferred to the others of the hunt group. <br /> <br /> <b>3rd:</b> A Soul Reborn<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Death 5<br /> There are two benefits to this attainment. The first is that the Knife can now trap the souls of those supernaturals that still have one. Vampires don\u2019t have one to take. Werewolves and other shapechangers do have a soul to be trapped, though the primal nature of these souls make it difficult for them to be trapped, adding a +1 to the difficulty. Werewolves will hunt those that steal their souls to the ends of the earth and beyond to rescue the soul. Mages have a soul that can be trapped. Changelings can be trapped. The living flame that serves as a Promethean\u2019s soul is said to be trappable, but to date no Knife has ever had one of these supernaturals as a choosen. Hunters are human and as such their souls can be trapped. Geists are strange beings, their souls linked to a second soul, so to speak. This dual soul nature makes it impossible for the Knifes to take their souls, as the blade can only hold one soul, not two. Mummies souls are untouchable, and any Knife that tries will themselves blasted by paradox. Demons don\u2019t have souls. Beasts are a strange thing, their souls hollowed out and replaced with the soul of the beast. It is possible to try to trap a Beast\u2019s soul, but don\u2019t expect it to remain trapped. Stories are told of a Knife who took a Beast\u2019s soul only to find themselves drawn into the Lair where they had to face the soul itself. Luckily the number of times a Beast has been the target is countable on one hand.<br /> The second benefit is the ability of the Knife to use the soul to help heal themselves when it is released to Stygia. When the release is done, the Knife takes a part of the soul and uses it to energize themselves, healing wounds and fatigue. This is similar to the Death 3 spell Devouring the Slain, but also heals wounds as well as willpower and mana. <br /> <br /> <i>The Stygian Blade (Imbued Item 4) </i>- This \u201csoulsteel\u201d blade is the weapon the Knife uses when they make their kills. The blade has the ability to \u201csteal the soul\u201d of the victim, holding it in its lattice till the ritual is done to release it. A blade can only hold one soul at a time in this manner and cannot be used to make another kill till the soul is released. The Blades are an Imbued Item with the Soul Jar (Death 2) persistent enchanted within it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mummies \u2013 The Arisen</b><br /> To the Arisen the Cemetery is a loose reminder of that strange dead land in which they went then they died and were reborn as an Arisen. Most look at the Cemetery with a measure of respect, knowing full well its dangers. Some whisper that some of the Deceived hide in the depths of the Cemetery, feeding on the alien necrotic energies, tended to by families of Ghuls and cults of slowly devolving mortals, plotting their strategies.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Arisen Cult \u2013 the Claws of the Shadowed Hawk</i></b><br /> The Claws of the Shadowed Hawk have existed for close to three centuries, based around four Deceived who, after a disastrous series of plans led to them losing all that they had done over the centuries before. Initially the four managed with what little they had, their remaining cultists helping move their bodies towards a new location but their enemies were several steps ahead of them and they lost dozens of their remaining cultists and a large portion of their remaining resources. Now it should be noted that the Arisen are aware of the border land now known as the Cemetery as well as the outer realm of Stygia. The four Deceived managed to locate a Shadowland and, locating the Shadow Gate within, moved everything they had through the portal and into the border march. They traveled towards Stygia and found an old set of tombs that they decided was the best place to set up shop. <br /> Initially they spent their time clearing the tombs, gathering the bodies to fuel fires and rituals, collecting the books, artifacts and other items and creating the tombs for the Arisen, the altar and ceremony room, as well as the living areas for the cultists. As time passed the mortal cultists started to devolve. The Arisen, aware of this possibility had their more learned members create talismans that would hold the effect at bay. They then used these talismans as gifts, given to those that performed well within the cult. The started recruiting members again from the Fallen World, using access points across the border march to setup contacts and associations. Needing fresh bodies, as well as supplies, arms and protection, the cult delved into various underworld activities slowly rebuilding themselves. <br /> Initially they supported local pirates and freebooters, as well as local bandits and other ne\u2019er-do-wells. Mortal dabblers in \u201cdark magics\u201d were also brought in to help bolster the growing priesthood of the cult. Those that were deemed unusable were left to devolve into ghuls. As the years passed by the Fallen World side shifted to trafficking slaves for cash, with some of the slaves being sent to the redoubt to become ghuls to help them grow their army. <br /> As the Fallen World continued to advance the cult kept its numbers at a constant state, recruiting new members when needed to keep their mortal followers going, and letting those they did not need devolve into feral ghuls that lived in the depths of the tomb as well as wandering the outskirts of it as guards. Over the passing years the Deceived slowly reworked their cult, forging them into the Claws of the Shadowed Hawk who worshipped the Deceived as four gods of ancient evil. <br /> In the modern nights the cult is hard at work conscripting criminals and other underworld and street people as its agents. Many of the people who are part of it are largely unseen by the general public, ignored and forgotten, which allows them to move about the city largely unchallenged. The Deceived use a combination of money, drugs, promises of power and actual low end magic being taught to keep their cultists in line and it works, most of the time. The four are now looking at finally expanding their operations with the upcoming Sothic Cycle and perhaps create a more powerful presence in the Fallen World, to which they have started to buy into a local corporation in order to create a secondary corporate styled cult over top of their more tribal one, (think the chrysaliss corporation from Cthulhutech). <br /> <br /> The tomb temple in the Cemetery sits close to the point where one has to shift into the outer realm of Stygia itself, where the older, more massive and alien tombs exist. The tomb itself is a vast thing, almost city like in its design with a central building and surrounding temples and store houses. The small buildings have become rectories, training areas, sleeping quarters and other such things for the cult, with the four Deceived having their own rooms deep within the massive central building. Patrolling the ruins around the tomb are various packs of ghuls, as well as feral hounds and other scavengers. Of note is the lack of Flayed in the area, though the cultists are ok with this. <br /> Fallen World locales tend to small shabby houses or apartments, though a couple of the gangs the cult controls have created temples to the four in underground locales and one old warehouse. The corporation the cult has slowly been infiltrating into is a tech company that back industrial robotics, and ships products worldwide, one of the primary reasons they were chosen. At this point numerous dock and factory workers unknowingly support the cult and a number of middle management are worshippers. The cult leaders are confident that they will have people in upper management within a couple years and are primed to put someone onto the board of directors through stock purchases by the end of the year.<br /> <br /> <b><i> The Claws of the Shadowed Hawk </i></b>(<b>Foundation</b> \u2013 <b>Tribal</b>: This cult is organized around the four Decieved who act as \u201cancient gods of evil\u201d whom the cult members have come to learn from in order to further their own greed for power. The members are inducted in grand ceremonies and group activities are frequent to keep them meshed in the cult. Those who defy the cult are punished, suffering from simple beatings to being fed to the devolved ghuls. Rewards come in the form of money, positions, servants, and arcane powers taught to the more enlightened.<b> Reach \u2013 4</b>: While the cult is based in the Cemetery where the four are entombed, they have access to several Tomb Gates which provide them access to several points across The City and its extended metropolitan area. <b>Grasp \u2013 4</b>: The cult has numerous ties across the city\u2019s underworld. The cult operates several hidden meth labs, as well as traffics in arms and bodies (both living and dead). Their activities often clash with other cults as well as other supernatural and mortal groups, but most of their interactions are merely seen as gang wars and left largely untouched. <b>Benefits \u2013 Blas\u00e9 </b>(the cult is used to the four Deceived being mobile, seeing them as gods and not questioning how they look, as gods can look like anything, and since they are gods of evil, death and shadow, they of course look nasty). <b>Inbred</b> (while new members are brought in on occasion, a number of the ghuls have procreated amongst themselves, providing the cult with a small army of near mindless, feral attack dog). <b>Ritualistic</b> (all the cults ceremonies are done big, from inductions to promotions to punishments; everything is done with all present so that the Deceived can bask in the members adoration at their divine nature). <b>Wrathful </b>(the ghuls of the cult are dangerous combatants and are often sacrificed as shock troops by the Deceived and their high priests when needed). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T23:59:19-08:00","id":834298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city?p=834031#post834031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mages \u2013 The Awakened</b><br /> <br /> <b>Death\u2019s Eyes</b><br /> <br /> <i>The dead leave many stories untold and so we search for them, to record them, pass them on, learn from them and grow from their knowledge and teachings.</i><br /> <br /> This legacy is based out in the Cemetery, seeing it as the perfect place to learn the state of death. Many of the legacy are looking into the secrets that were left by the Reapers and the Inquisitors, hunting for answers about what happened to the Outer Realm and border march that connects it to the Fallen World. They hunt for their answers with the dead interred within the border march and the spirits that still exist here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay,<i> how</i> are they different from Stone Scribes? Becuase to my reading - they are only a faction with slighlty diffrent Attianments at the end.<br /> <br /> Attainments that should not be possible, as mages <b>cannot</b> sustain &quot;fortress&quot; in Supernal Realm - in 2ED, Supernal can be just mass psychosis of mages. Legacy could be bounded with <i>Underworld</i> that way, but not Stygia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city?p=834031#post834031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Stygian Knives (Left Handed Legacy)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>They are simply Name Takers from Stone Scribes.<br /> <br /> I <i>could</i> see those two as sub-factions within Stone Scribes with slight Attainments, but the need polish a bit more. And if they are having Mysterium or Guardians as Orders, they cannot be Apostate - it's directly conflicting terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-21-2016, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T21:25:22-08:00","id":834825,"title":"","content":"Weirdly enough I never saw that .. sigh ... writers block must be in full if I am subconsciously pulling old memories of those legacies and re-writing them ... nertz ... ah well .. i shall step through em again. Just a note, the Stygia and Cemetery I reference isn't the supernal realm ... I know .. name confusion. I plan on fixing that soon, need to go through the four outer realms I made and give em lovely new names instead of Stygia, Pandemonium, Aether and the Primal Wild. Though Mage and Changeling do both use Arcadia as the name, though its not the same thing as of 2nd ed Mage. Ah well .. at least i know the juices are flowing through my brain if I am remembering stuff from the Legacies books that I read ages ago .. :-/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T20:03:24-07:00","id":855450,"title":"","content":"My most humble apologies to those who've been following this thread .. work has been rather annoying of late and as such my down time is spent nuking things in Warcrack, killing aliens in X-Com 2 or sailing the Unterzea in Sunless Sea ... i've got ideas... they are there .. just need a free moment to sit and let them forth. Again sorry about the lack of updates, please be patient.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:49:33-07:00","id":855966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/662429-the-city?p=855450#post855450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My most humble apologies to those who've been following this thread .. work has been rather annoying of late and as such my down time is spent nuking things in Warcrack, killing aliens in X-Com 2 or sailing the Unterzea in Sunless Sea ... i've got ideas... they are there .. just need a free moment to sit and let them forth. Again sorry about the lack of updates, please be patient.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the same boat as you, been doing the same. We appreciate the update, and rest assured you are not alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4662-xanbai","name":"Xanbai","avatar":